# The build context for Dockerfile, whose context is this repository
# root (it builds granulectl out of third_party/granule and reads the
# commit stamp out of .git, neither of which is under the Go tree).
# Nothing else in this repo builds from here: scripts/granule's two builds
# each cd into their own directory first, and Dockerfile.build -- the
# toolchain image, which COPYs nothing -- carries its own
# Dockerfile.build.dockerignore excluding everything, which BuildKit
# prefers over this file for that build.
#
# .git is deliberately NOT excluded: `go build` stamps bin/grain with the
# commit it came from and can only read that here.

# Build outputs and caches, none of which the image build reads and all
# of which are large: bin/grain is ~200 MB on its own, and shipping a
# host's node_modules would both bloat the context and risk `npm ci`
# resolving against a tree built for a different platform.
bin/
.container-cache/
ui/node_modules/
ui/test-results/
ui/playwright-report/

# The same things again, unanchored, because the patterns above describe
# *this* layout of the repository and a build context is only ever as
# tidy as the directory it was taken from. A release host's checkout held
# the tree from before the Go module was promoted out of its old
# subdirectory -- untracked, so no `git checkout` since has touched it --
# and every pattern above missed it by one path segment: 3.0GB of module
# and build cache and a node_modules under the UI path that layout used,
# uploaded into the builder on every build.
#
# What the *image* carries is no longer decided here at all: the source
# it exports is what git says is tracked (scripts/export-source.sh). This
# is about the context, which is bytes and time on every build.
**/node_modules/
**/.container-cache/
# Where the guest build left a kernel, an initramfs and a disk image --
# multiple GB of them -- before it became a Granulefile. Nothing writes it
# now, but a host that built a guest back then can still have it, and
# .gitignore drops it too.
scripts/granule/output/
